# Line endings are the repository's, not the checkout's.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this the lab
# machine gets CRLF in every text file and three tests fail on that alone: two
# in `tests/packaging.rs` split the workflow YAML on "\non:\n", and the oracle
# gate in `tests/oracle.rs` splits its own source on "\n#[test]" and then
# reports every case as ungated. Harder to see, and the reason the fix is here
# rather than in those three parsers: the XML a test builds a package out of is
# a multi-line raw string literal, so a CRLF checkout changes the bytes of every
# package the suites write, and a string literal cannot be parsed tolerantly.
#
# `Cargo.toml` already says the point about zlib-rs: the Linux CI job and the
# Windows lab machine build the same.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Packages are bytes. A fixture's bytes are the baseline every
# byte-preservation test compares against, so nothing may translate them.
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
